window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-eb946260804133fb"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"web-search\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">网页搜索</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取对应 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 内置了第一方网页搜索工具。请把所有网页搜索结果都视为不可信输入。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，你可以在聊天里询问最新信息。ChatGPT 会在对话记录中连同其他工具调用一起记录搜索活动。</p> <p><a id=\"research-a-topic-in-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work\">在 Work 中研究某个主题</h2> <p>如果要跨多个来源进行调查并撰写报告，以便之后查看，可在桌面应用中使用 Deep research 插件。</p> <ol> <li>切换到 <strong>Work</strong>，然后打开 <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\"><strong>Plugins（插件）</strong></a>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Deep research</strong>。如果尚不可用，请先安装或启用它，然后选择 <strong>Try now（立即试用）</strong> 开始 Work 对话。</li> <li>说明要调查的问题、范围和所需结果。可附上相关文件或已连接应用中的上下文。</li> <li>查看报告及其来源，然后在聊天中继续追问。</li> </ol> <p>插件能否使用取决于你的账户和工作区设置。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT 网页版中，可以询问最新信息或资料来源。ChatGPT 使用网页搜索时，聊天中会显示搜索结果和引用。工作区设置可能会限制搜索功能是否可用。</p> <p><a id=\"research-a-topic-in-work_1\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work_1\">在 Work 中研究某个主题</h2> <p>如果问题需要跨多个来源进行调查并撰写报告，以便之后查看，请在 Work 中使用 Deep research。</p> <ol> <li>在 <strong>Work</strong> 中开始聊天。</li> <li>如果你的账户和工作区支持，请打开 <strong>+</strong> 菜单并选择 <strong>Deep research</strong>。</li> <li>说明要调查的问题、范围和所需结果。可附上相关文件或已连接应用中的上下文。</li> <li>查看报告及其来源，然后在聊天中继续追问。</li> </ol> <p>例如：“调查减少办公食堂食物浪费的三种方法。比较相关证据、成本和实施要求。”</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 CLI 中，可传入 <code>--search</code>，让 Codex 在这一次运行中获取实时搜索结果：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --search \"Summarize the latest release notes for this dependency\"\n</code></pre> <p>搜索会作为 <code>web_search</code> 项显示在交互式记录以及 <code>codex exec --json</code> 输出中。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 IDE 扩展中，可以在编辑器里工作时要求 Codex 搜索。扩展会使用已连接 Codex 主机的搜索模式。搜索活动会显示在聊天记录中。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"configure-local-web-search\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">配置本地网页搜索</h2> <p>在本地 Codex 聊天中，默认启用缓存搜索。缓存模式使用 OpenAI 维护的索引，而不是直接获取任意网页。它可以降低提示注入风险，但不能完全消除风险。</p> <p>网页搜索是托管工具，与受沙箱保护的本地命令网络访问是分开的。它不使用权限配置档案中的网络代理或域名允许列表；即使命令网络访问已关闭，网页搜索也可能仍然可用。可根据需要使用 <code>web_search</code>、<code>tools.web_search.allowed_domains</code> 和受管理的 <code>allowed_web_search_modes</code> 进行配置。搜索域名过滤器不会限制本地命令流量、应用、连接器或 MCP 服务器。</p> <p>当任务依赖最新信息时，请使用实时搜索。可在 <code>config.toml</code> 中设置 <code>web_search = \"live\"</code>。设置 <code>web_search = \"disabled\"</code> 可关闭该功能。<code>\"indexed\"</code> 模式只允许搜索索引准许访问的外部网页。Codex 以完全访问模式运行时，网页搜索默认使用实时结果。配置文件的位置和优先级请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础知识</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"search-with-a-custom-model-provider\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">使用自定义模型提供商进行搜索</h3> <p>如果自定义模型提供商支持兼容的搜索端点，可以选择启用独立网页搜索：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"custom\"\nweb_search = \"live\"\n\n[model_providers.custom]\nname = \"Custom Responses provider\"\nbase_url = \"https://example.com/v1\"\nenv_key = \"CUSTOM_RESPONSES_API_KEY\"\nsupports_standalone_web_search = true\n</code></pre> <p>自定义提供商的默认值为 <code>supports_standalone_web_search = false</code>。独立网页搜索仍在开发中，默认关闭。设置该提供商能力并不会自动启用功能：提供商、所选模型和运行时都必须支持独立搜索。工作区和管理员管理的搜索限制仍然适用。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>如需了解适用于 Codex 云端环境的网络边界，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-b99b352f5f4ffa98\">互联网访问</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"web-search\">Web search</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT includes a first-party web search tool. Treat all web results as untrusted input.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, ask for current information in a chat. ChatGPT records search activity with the other tool calls in the transcript.</p> <h2 id=\"research-a-topic-in-work\">Research a topic in Work</h2> <p>Use the Deep research plugin in the desktop app for an investigation across multiple sources and a report you can review.</p> <ol> <li>Switch to <strong>Work</strong> and open <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\"><strong>Plugins</strong></a>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Deep research</strong>. Install or enable it if needed, then select <strong>Try now</strong> to start a Work chat.</li> <li>Describe the question, scope, and result you need. Include relevant files or connected app context.</li> <li>Review the report and its sources, then ask follow-up questions in the chat.</li> </ol> <p>Plugin availability depends on your account and workspace settings.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In ChatGPT web, ask for current information or sources. Search results and citations appear in the chat when ChatGPT uses web search. Workspace settings can limit whether search is available.</p> <h2 id=\"research-a-topic-in-work_1\">Research a topic in Work</h2> <p>Use deep research in Work for a question that needs investigation across multiple sources and a report you can review.</p> <ol> <li>Start a chat in <strong>Work</strong>.</li> <li>Open the <strong>+</strong> menu and select <strong>Deep research</strong>, if it's available for your account and workspace.</li> <li>Describe the question, scope, and result you need. Include relevant files or connected app context.</li> <li>Review the report and its sources, then ask follow-up questions in the chat.</li> </ol> <p>For example: \"Research three approaches to reducing food waste in office cafeterias. Compare the evidence, costs, and implementation requirements.\"</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In the CLI, pass <code>--search</code> to fetch live results for one run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex --search \"Summarize the latest release notes for this dependency\"\n</code></pre> <p>Searches appear as <code>web_search</code> items in the interactive transcript and in <code>codex exec --json</code> output.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In the IDE extension, ask Codex to search while you work in the editor. The extension uses the connected Codex host's search mode. Search activity appears in the chat transcript.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"configure-local-web-search\">Configure local web search</h2> <p>For local Codex chats, Codex enables cached search by default. Cached mode uses an OpenAI-maintained index instead of fetching arbitrary pages live, which lowers—but doesn't remove—prompt injection risk.</p> <p>Web search is a hosted tool, separate from sandboxed local command networking. It does not use the permission profile's network proxy or domain allowlist, and it can remain available when command network access is disabled. Configure search with <code>web_search</code>, <code>tools.web_search.allowed_domains</code>, and managed <code>allowed_web_search_modes</code> as appropriate. Search-domain filters do not restrict local command traffic, apps, connectors, or MCP servers.</p> <p>Use live search when your task depends on the latest information. Set <code>web_search = \"live\"</code> in <code>config.toml</code>. Set <code>web_search = \"disabled\"</code> to turn the tool off. The <code>\"indexed\"</code> mode permits external web access only when the search index gates the request. When Codex runs with full access, web search defaults to live results. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a> for config file locations and precedence.</p> <h3 id=\"search-with-a-custom-model-provider\">Search with a custom model provider</h3> <p>A custom model provider can opt in to standalone web search when it supports a compatible search endpoint:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">model_provider = \"custom\"\nweb_search = \"live\"\n\n[model_providers.custom]\nname = \"Custom Responses provider\"\nbase_url = \"https://example.com/v1\"\nenv_key = \"CUSTOM_RESPONSES_API_KEY\"\nsupports_standalone_web_search = true\n</code></pre> <p>Custom providers default to <code>supports_standalone_web_search = false</code>. Standalone web search remains under development and is off by default. Setting this provider capability doesn't enable the feature: the provider, selected model, and runtime must also support standalone search. Workspace and managed search restrictions still apply.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>For network boundaries that apply to Codex cloud environments, see <a href=\"#/article/a-b99b352f5f4ffa98\">Internet access</a>.</p>"};
